// The first .oddlg written, and for now the test card for the textbox engine.
//
// Everything the markup can do appears somewhere below, so a change that breaks
// one effect shows up by opening the tutorial rather than by reading the parser.

:: anchor=left size=20 pad=26 enter=type speed=42 line=1.4 pose=idle at=0.5,0.5 scale=1.0

@Advisor
Good morning, Minister. I am told you have **never run a country before**.

That is not a problem. It is *almost* the normal case.
---
@Advisor
:: pose=point at=0.32,0.5
The map is the game. Everything you can do, you do to a province: raise men in
it, build industry in it, fortify it, or take it from somebody who would rather
you did not.

Click a province and the panel on the left tells you what it is.
---
@Advisor
Three numbers decide whether you are winning, and only three.

{accent}Industry{/accent} is what you can build with. {accent=70}Manpower{/accent}
is what you can hold ground with. {accent=140}Unrest{/accent} is the one that
takes it all away again while you are looking somewhere else.
---
@Advisor
:: enter=type speed=30
Watch that third one. A province in {color=orange}open insurrection{/color} tells
you so, and it tells you {u}how many turns you have{/u} before it leaves.

You will get a warning. You will not always get a second one.
---
@Signals Officer
:: anchor=center enter=rise pose=hands_up at=0.5,0.46 scale=1.15
{shake}INCOMING{/shake}

The enemy fleet has been sighted off the cape. They are between us and the
convoy, and the convoy is carrying {b}the whole of the Third Army{/b}.
---
@Signals Officer
:: anchor=left enter=type speed=50 pose=point
A blockade closes a port. Nothing sails out of it and half its trade stops —
which is what a navy is *for*, in the long stretches between invasions.

Sink the ships sitting on your harbour, or route around them.
---
@Cryptographer
:: enter=type speed=22 pose=think at=0.68,0.5 flip=1
The intercept is only partly readable, Minister.

"...the offensive begins at {obf}0400 hours on the fourteenth{/obf}, and the
{obf}second{/obf} corps will {obf}cross at the ford below the mill{/obf}..."

We are working on the rest.
---
@Advisor
:: anchor=center enter=fade pose=shrug at=0.5,0.5 scale=1.0 flip=0
{rainbow}{b}That is the whole of it.{/b}{/rainbow}

Everything else is detail, and you will pick the detail up by losing to it.
---
@Advisor
:: anchor=left enter=type speed=42
One last thing, and it is the one nobody finds on their own.

{wave}Boats.{/wave} Armies cross water on transports, and a transport has to be
somewhere near the coast to load. If your invasion is not sailing, that is
almost always why.

Good luck, Minister.
